WEBVTT

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.210
Tomo...

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.130
Tomo?

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:26.920
Is he asleep?

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.790
He finally got to relax.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.240
He did push himself really hard.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:25.480
<i>Asura Cryin' 2</i>

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:12.260
"My Feelings for You Destroy the World"

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.730
Tomoharu.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.330
Nia...

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.750
Good morning.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.040
Takatsuki!

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:41.950
Y-yes?

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.690
I'm glad you're okay.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.010
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.980
Natsume-kun...

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.230
Good morning, Tomo.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.680
Looks like you're feeling better.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:57.760
You caused a lot of trouble by falling asleep the second we came back.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.840
Right, sorry.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.310
You were so heavy we couldn't take you upstairs.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.870
So that's why I was sleeping in the living room.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.320
This is the Meiotei, right?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.090
I thought it was destroyed in the explosion.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.260
Apparently, Naotaka sent the first world's Meiotei over with us.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.180
Pretty good, right?

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.400
It's more or less the same as the last Meiotei.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:23.450
Yeah.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.180
How are Shuri-san and Susugihara-san?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.110
Susugihara-san is in the hospital.

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.480
Shuri was taken away by members of the Dark Society.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.700
How is her condition? Is she alive?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.380
I don't know.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.380
But based on what happened...

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.000
Shuri-san...

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.510
This isn't the time to mope, Tomoharu.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.590
Don't forget why we came back to this world.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:49.730
I know.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.590
Nia, what should I do?

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:56.980
Tokiya is trying to destabilize the black hole in the central vortex...

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.980
...so he can go to the third world.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:03.960
A destabilized black hole would cause this world to vanish.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.970
Isn't that the same reason the first world was vanishing?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.420
Yes. In other words, Tokiya's attempts to create a third world...

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.670
...will destroy the second.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.180
President...

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.180
I won't let him do it.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:23.650
Let's go to the central vortex.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.460
Yeah.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.160
Hold on, Tomoharu.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.420
There's no point in going right now.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.540
In order to travel to the third world, Tokiya will have to take the fixed gate formed by an unstable black hole...

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.760
...planted in the central vortex when it stabilizes in 10 days.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:40.720
Fixed?

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:45.730
Yes. Gates to other worlds are highly unstable objects.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.510
The central vortex controls and fixes them.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.010
You really know a lot about this stuff, Nia-chan.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.650
Of course I do. I worked on the first world's experiment.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:00.990
So the showdown is in 10 days?

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.780
Yes. Tokiya probably won't do anything until then.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.020
Eat up, Tomoharu.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.210
We can't have you collapsing again.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.260
Uh, right.

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:17.020
Only an Asura Cryin' stands a chance against another Asura Cryin'.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.800
Asura Cryin'?

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.350
Don't play dumb.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.130
Didn't you make a contract with Kanade?

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.640
Oh, that's right! You did!

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.760
W-what?

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.970
Trying to hide in the confusion...

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.000
What? Wait a second...

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.460
T-that was the demon's contract?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.220
Was that it?

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:36.170
Yes.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:40.380
Thanks to you, I feel fantastic.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:44.440
Huh? But when we came back I wasn't...

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:48.160
In the first world, you had become a demon.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.650
Contracts can't be formed between demons.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:55.210
The contract wasn't properly established until we came back to the second world.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.680
Does that mean I have a daughter, too?

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.620
Yes, thanks to you we had an energetic child.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.090
Persephone!

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.170
That's it?

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:15.640
This is our daughter Persephone.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.010
Good morning, Tomoharu!

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.050
Good morning!

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.980
G-good morning, Higuchi, An.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.200
Why don't you explain the mysterious reappearance of the Meiotei?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.170
We can talk about that later.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.330
If we don't hurry, we'll be late.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.200
Okay, okay. I got it.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.070
How is Tokiya doing?

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.470
He's fine. He's recovering quite nicely.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.580
He should wake up soon.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.380
Are you okay?

00:06:56.170 --> 00:06:58.010
My master protected me.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.590
He suffered damage instead.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.010
It was a powerful blow.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:14.370
Yes. It's a miracle his injuries aren't any worse.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:17.730
This feels so strange.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:20.810
I really am a burial doll.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.510
Are you having regrets?

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.860
No, my body and mind feel lighter.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.930
The only thing I regret...

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.600
...is what happened to Aki-chan.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:34.770
I've always regretted it.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.310
If I had fought better...

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.070
If I had noticed Aki-chan's condition...

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.010
Thinking about it causes me so much pain.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.700
I don't know what I should do.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.940
But now I don't have to make any decisions.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.170
I can leave everything to Tokiya.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.830
Leave everything to him? And then what?

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.910
If we make it to the third world, I want to disappear...

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:04.610
...before we meet Aki-chan.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.010
That's why I'm working with Tokiya.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.180
I didn't realize you were so pathetic.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.370
Dying without understanding your own existence...

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.570
I'm amazed you're able to withstand something so stupid.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:18.510
Really?

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:22.480
Then why did you agree to become Tokiya's contracted demon?

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.450
Because I want to know.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.130
Know what?

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.150
Where did we demons come from?

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.130
How was this world formed and how will it end?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.330
I want to see and know all.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.950
My master said he would grant me this wish.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.930
You mean you don't love Tokiya?

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:44.470
No. I'm just curious.

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:49.200
Apparently, that was enough to make a contract and have a daughter.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:54.680
Now that I think about it, love is a fascinating subject as well.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:05.120
Your devotion and despair are both born from love.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:09.680
Please wake up soon, my master.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:16.900
President Toru...

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.290
Tomoharu Natsume.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.290
Oh, President Saeki.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.810
This can't be good, Tomo.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.800
So you made a contract?

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.720
T-there's a reason behind this...

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.820
Take them to the first student council office.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.820
Arrange an emergency student council presidents meeting.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:37.570
Yes, sir!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.070
W-what?

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.870
Susugihara-san, are you okay?

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.460
Amazingly, yes.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.980
Good.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.670
Things don't look good with him.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:57.740
Tomoharu Natsume.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:58.920
Y-yes.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:00.620
Let me be direct.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.680
Starting today, you will be the third student council president.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.430
Huh?

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.010
With Toru and Shuri gone, you're the only one.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.560
It's an emergency, and we didn't have a choice.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:14.470
W-wait a second. I can't be a student council president.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:15.940
What do you mean, you can't?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.040
Yes.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.500
There's something I have to do.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.670
Could that be saving this world?

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.700
Susugihara-senpai has filled me in on the situation.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:32.280
Isn't that the reason you became an Asura Cryin'?

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:33.710
That's different.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.180
You're saying because of this nobler purpose...

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:42.640
...you don't have time for the insignificant activities of a student council president?

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.230
Compared to saving the world...

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:51.770
...supporting and guiding the confused and disorderly students of Rakurowa High School doesn't matter?

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.000
No.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.870
I've come to realize...

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:03.060
...in the world I live in, there's no such thing as big or small.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.490
Good answer. You pass.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:11.810
I think that's a great mentality for the third student council president.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.050
Well said, Tomoharu Natsume...

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.830
...or rather, President Natsume.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.890
Let's go spread the word.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.220
Well, President Natsume?

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.700
Did you catch Tokiya Kagayaki?

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:32.920
No, not yet.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:35.920
What are you wasting time for?

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.980
Looks like the new third student council president is useless.

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.130
Don't mind her.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:46.360
President Rikka is just bored of living in the hospital.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:47.790
Shut up, Mahiwa!

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:50.950
With this eye, I can't even make you shut up.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:54.060
President Rikka, what's wrong with your eye?

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.280
There's nothing really wrong with it.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.560
I just can't see.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.370
What?

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.880
Rikka-chan, a little more to the right.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:05.880
Thank you!

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:08.430
When you say you can't see...

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.680
The injuries inflicted by the Picasso mask...

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.400
...blinded her in one eye.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:16.800
That's terrible...

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.370
What?

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:21.230
Are you worried about me?

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.200
Of course I am.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.100
You don't need to worry about me.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.480
I've got Himezasa and Mahiwa.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.460
And now that you're back, there's nothing I can't do.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:39.450
President Rikka...

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:43.240
I'll be fine, so go save the world or whatever.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.660
We're counting on you, President Natsume.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:46.890
Yes.

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:03.450
Where am I?

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:05.450
We're still in the second world.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.680
What's wrong?

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.030
I decided to do what I have to do.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:28.300
But...

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.390
Your heart can't keep up with reality?

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.830
Are you going to quit, then?

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:40.460
If you've made up your mind, you have to accept the consequences...

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.930
...no matter what they are.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:46.860
It's the only way to protect yourself from regret.

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:53.320
This is what I got for always doing what I had to do.

00:13:55.990 --> 00:14:00.260
Do you have any news about Shuri?

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:04.500
I woke up in a hospital bed.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.830
All I know is that she was taken away by the Dark Society.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:10.710
I see...

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:13.240
Shuri must be happy.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:14.150
What?

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:17.200
She has people who care for her so deeply.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:21.630
Shuri-san has done so much for me...

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.410
...and saved me so many times.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.300
She's very important to me.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.230
Then now more than ever, you have to do what you must.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:39.710
You have to make sure there's a world for Shuri to come back to.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:41.860
Right.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.980
When the GD's station was attacked...

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:51.800
...the altar trunks of Hisui, Bismuth, and Rhodonite were stolen.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.870
Was it the president?

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:55.090
Most likely.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:56.730
But why?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.670
I don't know.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:08.570
Let's do this.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:12.110
Come, Hagane.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:15.490
From the forge deeper than darkness...

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:18.660
...it is the steel tempered by the hammer of science.

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.860
Good, Hagane.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:03.760
It's a success.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:07.720
Hisui, Bismuth, and Rhodonite are mine.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:16.080
Master...

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.840
Let's go...

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.090
...to our utopia.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:30.270
Shuri?

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:33.000
Yes. Has she been here?

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:34.800
Unfortunately, no.

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.040
I see.

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.600
Did you make the right choice?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:41.660
What?

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:45.380
Tomoharu stopped the destruction of the first world.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:46.610
What?

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:50.670
Didn't you make only one choice?

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:57.020
You saved the first world, and now you're trying to save the second...

00:16:58.970 --> 00:16:59.840
I will save it.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:11.290
Nia's fast asleep.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.470
She must be exhausted.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:17.130
Are you sure it's okay for us to stay here?

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.720
Yes. It's late.

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.850
Ri-chan said the bath would be ready soon.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:24.540
The bath?

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:28.580
Yes. We have an open-air bath.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.580
R-really?

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:35.230
I bet you were just thinking about Takatsuki-san taking a bath.

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:36.310
No I wasn't!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:40.050
What are you so embarrassed about? You made a contract.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.330
But you've been passive this whole time.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.270
You really are a loser.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:47.630
Misao!

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:50.450
Sheesh.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:57.590
Um...

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.170
Go ahead.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.930
You first, Takatsuki.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:01.860
What?

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.620
Okay then...

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.260
Actually, wait.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.910
I'll go first.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:09.520
Okay.

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:11.970
Takatsuki...

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:13.970
Yes?

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.290
Well, uh...

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.470
Takatsuki.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:20.290
Yes?

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:23.170
Uh, Takatsuki...

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:29.380
You called my name many times...

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:33.090
...when I was about to vanish.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:37.640
I like it when you say my name.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.470
Takatsuki.

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:43.650
Yes?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.950
I like you, Takatsuki.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:47.950
I want to be with you forever.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:49.950
Yes.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.380
It's fine.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:04.670
In the end, Tomo will come back to me.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:07.420
Just as you stay by your master...

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.760
...I'll stay with Tomo.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.980
So this is the central vortex.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.770
What are you going to do, Tokiya?

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:22.930
The central vortex hasn't stabilized yet.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:25.420
We do not have an igniter, either.

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:28.590
I don't need either of those.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.730
I'll go to the third world right now.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.970
Come, Hagane.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:41.030
Hisui, Bismuth, Rhodonite!

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.310
The central vortex is moving.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:08.890
Do it.

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:27.670
Good, just like that.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.550
Run it out of control!

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:39.970
More.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:41.650
Push it to the limit!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.580
Is this...?

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:58.050
It's the gate to the third world.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:00.280
Let's go.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:26.870
What is this?

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:29.690
Can you see that?

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:33.770
Why is that black hole out of control?

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:38.410
No...

00:21:38.720 --> 00:21:41.080
Why is this happening so soon?

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:42.630
That's...

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:47.230
The world is vanishing.

00:23:21.020 --> 00:23:22.720
Waiting for dawn.

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:23.610
Lies.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:24.790
Stay away.

00:23:24.910 --> 00:23:25.430
Lies.

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:26.840
Don't leave me.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:27.480
Lies.

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:29.770
But it's not a lie.

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:34.990
"Despair at the Diverging Past and Causality"
